{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Em8BNqbU86yb1NRXj2opaT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# WI-237 — Ownership claims scan: ignore integration-reachable commits\n2\t\n3\t**Branch:** dualplan-routing-fix · **Filed:** 2026-07-19 (field finding — the\n4\tWI-229 pre-merge quarantine) · **BuildTier:** medium · **SafetyClass:**\n5\thigh-risk (recovery/ownership reconstruction, SR-064 family).\n6\t\n7\t## Why\n8\t\n9\tReconcile derives a train's claimed WIs by scanning its commits; a claim on a\n10\tWI the train has not reserved quarantines it fail-closed\n11\t(`claims-unreserved-wi`). Field event 2026-07-19 (run `20260719T105727`): the\n12\towner merged the development branch INTO train `p0-g3-WI-229-3999` to preempt\n13\tknown integration conflicts before stage 3 — a content-only sync — and the\n14\tscan read the imported `WI-226:`/`WI-227:`/… commit subjects as foreign\n15\tclaims, quarantining the attested, stage-3-ready train at launch. Recovery\n16\trequired manual state surgery (retire train + release reservation; safe only\n17\tbecause the train tip happened to be fully integration-contained). The scan's\n18\tsuspicion is correct for genuinely ambiguous trains, but a commit **already\n19\treachable from the integration ref** is integrated history, not a claim this\n20\ttrain is making — treating it as one makes any owner sync/merge into a\n21\treserved train a quarantine trap.\n22\t\n23\t## Scope\n24\t\n25\tWhen deriving a train's claims, exclude commits reachable from the\n26\tintegration ref (`git rev-list <tip> ^<integration-head>` bounds the scan, or\n27\tthe equivalent merge-base filtering) so only the train's OWN novel commits\n28\tcan claim WIs. A genuine foreign claim in novel commits still quarantines\n29\texactly as today. Document the now-sanctioned owner resync (\"merging the dev\n30\tbranch into a reserved train is content-sync, not claiming\") in the\n31\tPROCESS_OPTIONS unattended section (byte-budget guard applies) and the spec\n32\tof record for the dispatcher's reconcile.\n33\t\n34\t**Non-goals:** no relaxation of duplicate-reservation or unreadable-metadata\n35\tquarantines; no auto-resync of trains; no change to reservation metadata.\n36\t\n37\t## Done-when\n38\t\n39\tRegressions prove: a train with the dev branch merged in (imported foreign-WI\n40\tcommit subjects, all integration-reachable) reconciles and resumes instead of\n41\tquarantining; a train whose NOVEL commits claim an unreserved WI still\n42\tquarantines with the same reason; the WI-229 field shape (reservation base\n43\tpredating the merge) is the driven scenario. Suite green.\n44\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dacfaa29-0f09-4cde-a460-8dc79d700902","uuid":"d250f100-ff04-4f47-99ef-31f7264bdffc","timestamp":"2026-07-19T16:23:22.885Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-trains\\4-g3-WI-237-a515\\docs\\specs\\WI-237.md","content":"# WI-237 — Ownership claims scan: ignore integration-reachable commits\n\n**Branch:** dualplan-routing-fix · **Filed:** 2026-07-19 (field finding — the\nWI-229 pre-merge quarantine) · **BuildTier:** medium · **SafetyClass:**\nhigh-risk (recovery/ownership reconstruction, SR-064 family).\n\n## Why\n\nReconcile derives a train's claimed WIs by scanning its commits; a claim on a\nWI the train has not reserved quarantines it fail-closed\n(`claims-unreserved-wi`). Field event 2026-07-19 (run `20260719T105727`): the\nowner merged the development branch INTO train `p0-g3-WI-229-3999` to preempt\nknown integration conflicts before stage 3 — a content-only sync — and the\nscan read the imported `WI-226:`/`WI-227:`/… commit subjects as foreign\nclaims, quarantining the attested, stage-3-ready train at launch. Recovery\nrequired manual state surgery (retire train + release reservation; safe only\nbecause the train tip happened to be fully integration-contained). The scan's\nsuspicion is correct for genuinely ambiguous trains, but a commit **already\nreachable from the integration ref** is integrated history, not a claim this\ntrain is making — treating it as one makes any owner sync/merge into a\nreserved train a quarantine trap.\n\n## Scope\n\nWhen deriving a train's claims, exclude commits reachable from the\nintegration ref (`git rev-list <tip> ^<integration-head>` bounds the scan, or\nthe equivalent merge-base filtering) so only the train's OWN novel commits\ncan claim WIs. A genuine foreign claim in novel commits still quarantines\nexactly as today. Document the now-sanctioned owner resync (\"merging the dev\nbranch into a reserved train is content-sync, not claiming\") in the\nPROCESS_OPTIONS unattended section (byte-budget guard applies) and the spec\nof record for the dispatcher's reconcile.\n\n**Non-goals:** no relaxation of duplicate-reservation or unreadable-metadata\nquarantines; no auto-resync of trains; no change to reservation metadata.\n\n## Done-when\n\nRegressions prove: a train with the dev branch merged in (imported foreign-WI\ncommit subjects, all integration-reachable) reconciles and resumes instead of\nquarantining; a train whose NOVEL commits claim an unreserved WI still\nquarantines with the same reason; the WI-229 field shape (reservation base\npredating the merge) is the driven scenario. Suite green.\n","numLines":44,"startLine":1,"totalLines":44}}}
