{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdBmHp6yprAP1G7ZkLZ79","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-237 is complete. Summary of what I did on train `4-g3-WI-237-a515`:\n\n## The fix\n**`project-trajectory/scripts/agent_dispatch.py` — `train_branch_evidence`**: the claim scan (`git log base..tip`) now bounds with `^<integration-head>`, so only the train's **own novel commits** (in `base..tip` and *not* reachable from `refs/heads/llm/integration`) can claim a WI. A commit already reachable from the integration ref is integrated history, not a claim.\n\nThis closes the WI-229 field trap: an owner merging the development branch **into** a reserved train (a content-only sync to preempt stage-3 conflicts) imported the integrated commits' `WI-226`/`WI-227`/… trailers, which the scan read as foreign claims and fail-closed-quarantined (`claims-unreserved-wi`) the attested, stage-3-ready train. The bound lives in one place, so reconcile, the early-end release, and the blocked-disposition path all read the train's own evidence consistently. No signature change; absent integration ref = prior behavior.\n\n## Regression tests (`tests/test_agent_loop_recovery.py`)\n- **`test_owner_dev_merge_into_reserved_train_is_not_a_foreign_claim`** — the exact WI-229 field shape (reservation base predating the merge) reconciles to `ready-to-integrate`, no quarantine.\n- **`test_novel_foreign_claim_after_owner_sync_still_quarantines`** — the exclusion is *precise*: a genuinely novel `WI-999` claim on top still quarantines, naming only the novel WI, never the merged-in dev WIs.\n\nThe existing rogue-claim quarantine test still passes.\n\n## Docs\n- Dispatcher reconcile spec of record (`docs/specs/parallel-wi-dispatch.md` recovery table) and the `PROCESS_OPTIONS.md` unattended crash-safety section now document the sanctioned owner resync. Byte-budget flag: **PROCESS_OPTIONS.md 158,094 → 158,557 (+463)**; baseline re-stamped in the